1
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:03,580
Thank you.

2
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:34,177
I couldn't believe Ken went with Aro Kunemon,
but at least he had me to rescue him.

3
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:38,497
Daemon showed up and that creepy Oikawa
dude was just going to hand Ken over to him.

4
00:01:38,580 --> 00:01:40,117
That's when I sprang into action.

5
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:43,297
We didn't really need the help, but I was
glad when the others finally showed up.

6
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:44,437
Took him long enough.

7
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:47,357
Daemon could open digital
ports anytime he wanted to.

8
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:51,097
So Kauri said we should send him to the
dark ocean instead of the digital world.

9
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:52,277
Easier said than done.

10
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:55,437
Ken had to use the dark power
still deep inside him to

11
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:57,697
open the gate and banish Daemon
from the face of the earth.

12
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:59,662
Now that's what I call teamwork.

13
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,100
Black O 'Greymon time.

14
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:07,650
O 'Greymon.

15
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:10,790
Yes, sir.

16
00:02:10,873 --> 00:02:11,837
We're organizing and cleaning.

17
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:14,802
Any cleaner in the place
would be a soap factory.

18
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,977
Yeah, I've already
organized that drawer, sir.

19
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:20,497
I've got the paper cuts
to show for it, too.

20
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:22,577
Sorry, I just need to find something.

21
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:23,857
I'll get the bandages.

22
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:26,537
But I'm actually going to miss
the office over the holidays.

23
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,177
It's always so nice and quiet.

24
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:29,090
Found it!

25
00:02:29,173 --> 00:02:30,003
See what I mean?

26
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,633
There, this is the guy.

27
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,367
Oh, he gives me the willies.

28
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:34,760
It is him!

29
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:37,357
Well, he was at work
until just a few days ago.

30
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:39,757
But yesterday and today,
he didn't show up at all.

31
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,637
He didn't even call in or anything.

32
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:42,550
Thanks, Dad.

33
00:02:42,633 --> 00:02:44,357
Would it be all right
if we kept this picture?

34
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,969
Of course, go right ahead.

35
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:48,315
But don't do anything dangerous, okay?

36
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,740
Uh-huh. Huh? Hmm.

37
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,677
Why do I think that's exactly
what you're going to do?

38
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:55,700
He looks just like an
ordinary person. Yeah?

39
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:59,137
Then why is he able to control
Arukenemon and Mummymon?

40
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,720
I don't care what he is.

41
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:02,526
I just want to shut him down.

42
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,280
Ah, Mount Fuji.

43
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:06,440
This world can be beautiful.

44
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:09,320
But soon I'll claim my true prize.

45
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:12,500
Arukenemon, I believe that opens in.

46
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,019
Well, it does now.

47
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:19,777
If you're through playing
around, it's time to get to work.

48
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:23,257
This is a classic case of mass
hallucination, plain and simple.

49
00:03:23,340 --> 00:03:24,357
What are you talking about?

50
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,877
Buildings have been destroyed!

51
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:29,237
It's obviously a government
conspiracy to cover up a UFO crash!

52
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:33,097
What I'm saying, I mean, I'm just
saying that the destruction is real,

53
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:35,217
but a mass hallucination caused it to seem

54
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,657
that the destruction
was caused by monsters.

55
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:40,152
The government got to you too, didn't it?

56
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:43,020
If only Digimon were this deluded.

57
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:46,977
The digital world would fall at
our feet like a ripe little plum.

58
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,380
To them, Digimon and UFOs
are exactly the same thing.

59
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,917
It's just something they're
afraid to admit exists.

60
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:53,960
But think,

61
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:59,280
if there's such a commotion now, wait
till all those dark spores begin to bloom.

62
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:03,720
There we go.

63
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:04,920
I'm all done.

64
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:10,737
Are you saying that you're done with
your homework for the whole winter break?

65
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:11,680
Mm-hmm.

66
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,374
Honey, that's amazing.

67
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,880
I'll say it is. Crazy, even.

68
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:19,777
I mean, he was just returned from that
whole kidnapping incident last night.

69
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:22,037
That's because he's
such a smart little boy.

70
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:24,837
You know, the press is sure to show
up again to talk about the kidnapping,

71
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:28,567
and we can get more attention
by telling them how smart he is.

72
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:29,590
Hon,

73
00:04:29,673 --> 00:04:32,657
maybe he'll become a media darling
just like that Ken Ichijoji,

74
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:35,120
and then we'll get on TV. You bet.

75
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:38,516
Then everyone will know we're
the parents of a genius.

76
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:40,290
Insects.

77
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:43,250
Yes.

78
00:04:43,333 --> 00:04:44,429
That's the man, all right.

79
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:46,200
He gives me the willies.

80
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:48,517
Yeah, that's what
everybody says about him.

81
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,717
Hey, didn't you need to be someplace?

82
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:51,740
You were right.

83
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:54,357
Fill me in when I get back, okay?

84
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,657
Now feel free to make yourselves at home.

85
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:57,570
Thanks!

86
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:58,780
See you later.

87
00:05:00,180 --> 00:05:01,420
Oh, wait. Here.

88
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:06,019
Looks like Mom's done some
investigating of her own.

89
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:10,000
Didn't you know TK's mom is
a newspaper reporter? Really?

90
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:12,940
Yeah. And look. Wow.

91
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,340
Uh, what is it?

92
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:16,051
Oh, is it a grocery list?

93
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:18,937
No, Goofy, it's the names and
addresses of the kidnapped kids.

94
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:21,480
Your mom does good work, TK. Ken?

95
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:24,377
We've got to save them
all before it's too late.

96
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:25,800
You can count me in.

97
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:30,097
We can't allow those children to
become drawn into evil the way I was.

98
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:32,177
Right, all those kids are depending on us.

99
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:33,090
Yeah!

100
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:36,917
Hey, I don't mean to cause trouble,
but just what is the plan anyway?

101
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,357
Well, um...

102
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,517
Let's split up and go
meet with those kids.

103
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:44,482
If we act quickly, maybe we can
stop the dark spores from growing.

104
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:45,817
What are we waiting for?

105
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:46,730
Let's go!

106
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:51,537
That Noriko girl should be
home any time now, right?

107
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:52,450
Right.

108
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:58,802
Guys, isn't that her,
like, right in front of us?

109
00:05:58,920 --> 00:05:59,750
Oh, yeah.

110
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:03,377
Get away from me.

111
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:04,519
You're disgusting.

112
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:07,057
She kicked it.

113
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:09,200
I guess she is evil, huh?

114
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:12,197
Yeah, maybe it's not even
worth talking to her.

115
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:15,339
It looks like the Dark Spore
has already taken hold.

116
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:18,980
We have to at least try.

117
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,479
I don't even like to fight Digimon.

118
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:24,819
What will we do if we're
forced to fight other kids?

119
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:27,980
What do you want?

120
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:29,350
No!

121
00:06:29,433 --> 00:06:31,620
Now go away and don't come back!

122
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:35,054
Wait, ma 'am, just listen for a minute.

123
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:38,700
Man, how do people get
any encyclopedias sold?

124
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,740
Sorry, guys, I tried.

125
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:41,920
I know, Davis.

126
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,837
It's not your fault she got angry.

127
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:44,750
Yeah.

128
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,000
She needs some catnip.

129
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:49,966
Well, let's try the next one.

130
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:53,210
Insects.

131
00:06:53,293 --> 00:06:55,040
Stupid little meaningless bugs.

132
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:57,500
They need to be squashed.

133
00:06:58,600 --> 00:07:01,160
Okay, I'll throw in
some oysters, broccoli,

134
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:04,381
a quart of buttermilk, and
just a dash of vinegar.

135
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:11,740
Why do people find this
cold, wet gunk pretty?

136
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:14,277
Do you think it'll cause
any problems tomorrow?

137
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:16,717
Well, I suppose anything's
possible, Arukenemon.

138
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,480
Go put the snow chains on the tires. What?

139
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:20,720
Why should I?

140
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:23,140
Because you're annoying me. Fine.

141
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:27,260
Because you're annoying me.

142
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,710
Huh?

143
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,580
Was that a shooting star?

144
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:48,870
Ken,

145
00:07:48,953 --> 00:07:50,577
I know you're going to hate hearing this,

146
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:53,377
but I really don't think
we're going to be able to

147
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:56,342
remove the dark spores
from those kidnapped kids.

148
00:07:56,460 --> 00:08:00,737
I'm thinking that Oikawa is probably
the only person that can extract them,

149
00:08:00,820 --> 00:08:04,017
but we may be We'll be able
to use that to our advantage.

150
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:08,137
He's probably got something specific planned
and will come for them sooner or later,

151
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:09,050
so...

152
00:08:09,133 --> 00:08:12,080
So if we watch them, we'll
catch Owikawa. Right.

153
00:08:13,020 --> 00:08:14,260
That's a great idea.

154
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:16,737
We can ask Tai and the
others to help us out, too.

155
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:17,650
Sounds good.

156
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:18,980
I'm sorry, Ken.

157
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:21,837
I know you'd hoped we could
save those kids before...

158
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,577
You really don't need to worry about me.

159
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:25,080
I'll be fine. Mm-hmm.

160
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,274
You ever not get mail?

161
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,217
It's from my brother.

162
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:33,720
All right, let's get
started on this plan, guys.

163
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:35,437
They're nearby.

164
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:36,402
I can sense it.

165
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:40,380
Perhaps now I will finally
find the answers I seek.

166
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:46,380
Don't my teddy bear mind.

167
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:52,920
I already told you, you can't have it.

168
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:56,600
Hey, you lazybones, wake up! What?

169
00:08:57,420 --> 00:08:59,597
We have a visitor. Find out who.

170
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:00,562
Oh, Teddy bear?

171
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:19,160
It's Blackwar Greymon! Oh, no.

172
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,360
Oh, yes.

173
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:40,677
Okay, everybody's got their assignments
about who they're supposed to follow.

174
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,137
Make sure you stick close to them.

175
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:44,777
We don't want Oikawa sneaking
in when we're not looking.

176
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:48,277
While we're following those kids, Tai
and Kari are going to the digital world.

177
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:49,680
Okay, see you soon.

178
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:53,920
Look at all this destruction.

179
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:57,340
Any idea what caused it? No.

180
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:59,280
Hey, Tai! Kari!

181
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,737
Sorry to call you into the
digital world like this,

182
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:04,317
but you're in real serious danger.

183
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:06,177
You know who is up to something.

184
00:10:06,260 --> 00:10:07,280
Twitch my tail.

185
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:08,417
You don't mean...

186
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,360
not Black War Greymon.

187
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:14,377
Remember when Azulonmon
gave up some of his

188
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:17,720
power to help us fight
in the real world? Well,

189
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:20,017
when Gennai gave that power to all of us,

190
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,677
the defenses of the digital
world were weakened.

191
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:24,701
With the balance thrown off here,

192
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:27,617
there's not much that can stand
in the way of Black War Greymon.

193
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:31,000
I guess we've got no choice
but to try and find a way.

194
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:32,860
Hey, look!

195
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:33,920
What is it?

196
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,260
Looks like Mount Fuji.

197
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:38,562
That's because it is Mount Fuji.

198
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:42,737
Do you mean that Black War
Greymon is in the real world?

199
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:44,900
That's what Azulonmon told us.

200
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:47,020
We knew we had to call you guys.

201
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:49,817
But we don't have the
strength to defeat him.

202
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:54,841
Agumon got more power from Azulonmon, but
there wasn't enough power for anyone else.

203
00:10:55,380 --> 00:10:58,557
Do you think you're up to
fighting Black War Greymon, buddy?

204
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,540
If he really, really wants to.

205
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:01,761
All right, then.

206
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:03,500
Let's go find him, guys.

207
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:07,620
Be careful with Black War Greymon,
but you can't let him win.

208
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:11,380
So, we meet again.

209
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:14,020
And this time, we're ready for you.

210
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,580
Ready to be defeated again, you mean.

211
00:11:19,740 --> 00:11:22,557
So, this is the infamous
Black War Greymon.

212
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:25,360
Just what do you hope to accomplish here?

213
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:28,220
I wish to look upon
the face of my creator.

214
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:33,807
You've come all this way to see
what you've already seen then.

215
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:37,520
I gave you life from just
the tiny hairs on my head.

216
00:11:37,660 --> 00:11:40,280
Perhaps, but who gave you life? Huh?

217
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:43,000
And who is your creator, Mummymon?

218
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:44,800
Oh, Wild!

219
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:46,200
It was me.

220
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:47,630
Huh?

221
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:52,180
I made both of these Digimon
by turning my DNA into data.

222
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:57,320
So you see, BlackwarGreymon, I am the
creator you've been searching for.

223
00:11:57,540 --> 00:12:01,011
Then I am a product of the real
world, not the digital one.

224
00:12:01,140 --> 00:12:01,970
Interesting.

225
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:05,217
Yes, I think you've gotten
what you came for, haven't you?

226
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:06,520
So now leave us.

227
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:10,249
It's all beginning to
make sense to me now.

228
00:12:10,380 --> 00:12:12,797
I've been searching for
answers in the digital world,

229
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:15,297
trying to find the
meaning of my existence,

230
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:18,257
but have been able to find
nothing to ease my pain.

231
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:20,137
And now I know why.

232
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:24,800
I was created from you, just
like Arukenymon and Mamemon were.

233
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:29,060
We're a part of the real world,
foreign to the digital world.

234
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:31,360
We do not belong there.

235
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:34,860
If you're done
philosophizing, then goodbye.

236
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:36,680
I'll leave.

237
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:38,340
As soon as I'm done here.

238
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:41,280
Foreign objects must be eliminated.

239
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:43,197
What are you talking about?

240
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,520
I'm not a foreign object. But you are.

241
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:48,457
You belong in neither the
digital world nor the real world.

242
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:50,305
You upset the balance of both.

243
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,980
This guy's talking crazy.

244
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:55,396
Do you want me to, uh, take
care of him for you, boss?

245
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,110
Boss?

246
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:59,720
A foreign object?

247
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:03,300
I give you life and this
is how you repay me!

248
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:04,900
What's going on?

249
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:09,560
Weep! Weep! Weep!

250
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:12,770
You.

251
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,380
I remember you.

252
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:16,180
Let's talk about this.

253
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:18,124
There is nothing to talk about.

254
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:20,740
Hey, look out!

255
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:25,160
